<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10181"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 1:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well what is on my mind at the moment is .  <BR>Who was the three &#34;dude&#34; BTK wrote about in his letter?  <BR>Any of them with the last name RADER???  <BR>Any of them named Paul? Jeffery? &#40;Jeff&#41; or William? &#40;Bill&#41;.&#40;his brothers names&#41;  <BR>Were any of them Dennis Raders brothers?  <BR> <BR>It was stated that two of the &#34;dued큦&#34; was brothers, one was 19 at the time the other was 26 years old..  <BR> <BR>Due to the article &#40;se further down this post&#41; Jeff Rader would have been 19 in 1974-75, so could he have been one of the dudes? Now we need to find out if one of the rader brothers was born in 1948-49!  <BR>Paul Rader, in the info &#40;at the bottom of this post&#41; said to be born prob. 1948, SO is he the 26 yesr old dude?  <BR> <BR>Here is quotes from early on newsreports:  <BR> <BR>&#34;I write this letter to you for the sake of the tax payer as well as your time. Those three dude you have in custody are just talking to get publicity for the Otero murders. They know nothing at all. I did it by myself and with no ones help. There has been no talk either. Let&#39;s put this straight... .&#34;  <BR> <BR>&#34;The writer of the letter would have had to be inside the house when the crime was committed or participated in the crime,&#34; said Floyd Hannon, then chief of police.  <BR> <BR>Police maintain that other suspects connected with the case have not been ruled out, despite the  <BR>existence of the letter. The most prominent suspect is a 19-year-old who confessed to the crime and  <BR>then implicated his 26-year-old brother and another man, age 30. All three are under psychiatric care  <BR>in separate hospitals.  <BR> <BR>&#34;The 19-year-old gave us details of the murder but none that he couldn&#39;t have read in the newspaper,&#34;  <BR>sighed Hannon. &#34;That&#39;s one of the problems in the case - too much publicity.&#34;  <BR> <BR>When asked if the 19-year-old or the other two men were still under suspicion, Detective Maj. Bill  <BR>Cornwell replied: &#34;At this time, we have insufficient evidence. We&#39;re not saying they are and we&#39;re  <BR>not saying they aren&#39;t.&#34;  <BR> <BR> <BR>And then there is Dennis Raders cousin Dean Rader.  <BR>Could be this man , he was released from jail marts 24th 2004.  <BR>He was born 1954, could he have been one of the dueds?  <BR>&#40;I have heard that he raped his own daughter, don큧 know if it is true.Also read on Dennis raders daughters homepage that HER cousin died in 1996 any connection to Dean Newton Rader?&#41;  <BR> <BR><a href="http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:nnqapWln6PoJ" target=_top>http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:nnqapWln6PoJ</a>: docnet.dc.state.ks.us/kasper2/offender.asp%3Fid%3D 55023&#43;%22rader,&#43;dean&#43;newton%22&#43;&#43;%2B24&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=lan g_en  <BR> <BR> <BR>his<a href="http://www.kansascity.com/mld/kansascity/news/nati" target=_top>http://www.kansascity.com/mld/kansascity/news/nati</a> on/11017252.htm  <BR>Article about dennis Raders brother Jeff Rader:  <BR>Jeff Rader is a plumber, 50, nine years younger. Unlike his balding older brother, he&#39;s got a full head of hair, brown and curly.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:0MJ1HZyQOfAJ" target=_top>http://64.233.183.104/search?q=cache:0MJ1HZyQOfAJ</a>: familytree.paradigmpress.net/f_25f.htm&#43;%22paul&#43;rad er%22&#43;%2Bwichita&amp;hl=en  <BR> <BR>Children:  <BR>Rader, William {I4242}  <BR>b. C. 1946  <BR>Gender: Male  <BR> <BR>Rader, Paul {I4243}  <BR>b. C. 1948 prob. Wichita, KS  <BR>Gender: Male  <BR> <BR>Rader, Dennis {I4244}  <BR>b. C. 1950 prob. Wichita, KS  <BR>Gender: Male  <BR> <BR>Rader, Jeffrey {I4245}  <BR>b. C. 1952 prob. Wichita, KS  <BR>Gender: Male  <BR>  <BR>Skov <BR>Username: Skov <BR> <BR>Registered: 12-2004 <BR> Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 6:29 am:      <BR> <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR>I found this info on the Rader family.  <BR> <BR> <BR>Father- William E. Rader &#40;deceased, 1996&#41;  <BR>Mother- Dorothea M. Rader  <BR>Brothers- Paul &#40;1947&#41;, Bill Rader &#40;1949&#41;, Jeff &#40;1955&#41;,  <BR> <BR>Obituary &#40;Wichita Eagle on Dec. 29, 1996&#41;  <BR>William E. &#34;Bill&#34; Rader,74, retired KG&amp;E Ripley Generating Station plant operator; died Friday, Dec. 27, 1996. Survivors: wife, Dorothea: sons, Dennis, Jeff, both of Wichita, Paul of Falun, Bill of Climax; brothers, Ted of Wichita, Don of Grove, OK, Wallace of Mitchell, IN; eight grandchildren.  <BR> <BR>1948-1963 William E. Rader, held various positions for KG&amp;E Fireman, lineman, etc.  <BR>1960 Dorothea M. Rader, bookeeper, Leekers IGA  <BR> <BR> <BR>This means that the brothers in 1974 would bee:  <BR> <BR>Paul:27 years  <BR>Bill &#40;william&#41;: 25  <BR>Jeff &#40;jerrery&#41; : 19  <BR> <BR>SO it is possible that some of thise brothers were the &#34;dude큦&#34; BTK wrote about in his letter.  <BR>Did BTK want to save his brothers?  <BR>OR did his brothers want to, or was threthened to, save Dennis?  <BR> <BR>I am grasping at straws, I know, but I cantlet it go for som reason...  <BR> <BR>Any thoughts?  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
