</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 7:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Itty  <BR> <BR>Do you have a link for Ghostiesannex? <BR> <BR>We might as well face the fact that none of us are going to be satisfied until we know for sure that: 1&#41; Rader acted totally on his own. or 2&#41;he if he had help, they are apprehended as well.  <BR> <BR>  <BR>The main reason I started following the catchbtk site was to help to stop more killings &#40;which at least one shrink suggested was in the offing&#41;. Until we are sure Rayder acted alone there is no guarantee of that. The &#34;three dude theory&#34;, to me is not limited to the three guy&#39;s questioned for the Otero murders, that&#39;s the starting point. They need to be accounted for, the question of the car/cars in the Davis/Hedge murders needs to be resolved, and all murders that BTK was responsible for need to be linked to BTK in case they point to more than one person being involved. <BR> <BR> Another suspect area would be the puzzles, do they contain evidence of more than one murderer. Theoretically, unless one letter or number has been used in more than one clue already, there is an &#34;exhaustable&#34; amount of information in the puzzles. If letters and numbers are used more than once already then there might be a ton of clues running diagnally and backwards. <BR> <BR>Other things that I would &#39;like&#39; to see addressed: <BR> <BR>Who knew what and when. <BR> <BR>Rader&#39;s service record, and does it have any connection to the Oteros. <BR> <BR>Rader&#39;s connection to any of the victims. <BR> <BR>Was there impropriety involved with his involvement with youth organizations? <BR> <BR>And now we have to ask: whats the official answer to the question &#34;what does a woman&#40;or anyone else&#41; do when someone comes to the door and shows a badge &#40;apparently, of which, there are a lot more variety than I ever knew&#41;?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
