<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10445"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 10:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is the lates I found out supporting BTK knew the three dudes: <BR> <BR>Bottomline is that BTK sent his first letter about the 3 dudes 2 days after the first two dudes was in custody and 6 days BEFORE!!! the third &#34;dude&#34; was in custody.   <BR> <BR>here is a timeline 1974: <BR> <BR>oct 8th :  the two dudes who were brothers are &#34;picked up&#34; and in custody <BR> <BR>oct 12th :  BTK letter mentionig &#34;the three dude&#34; is called in by phone by BTK himself, to Don Granger , Wichita Eagle the letter is picked up by WPD at the Wichita Public Libarary hidden in a Technical enginering textbook <BR> <BR>0ct 18th :  the third &#34;Dude&#34; is picked up and in custody <BR> <BR>Oct. 24th :  police placed a personal classified advertisement in an attempt to contact &#34;B.T.K.&#34;  <BR> <BR>Dec 11th :  For the fist time info about the BTK letter about the Oteros murders, the &#34;Monster&#34; and the three &#34;dudes&#34; are released by newspaper&#34; The Wichita Sun&#34;  <BR> <BR>skov <BR>  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
