<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10456"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 11:41 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://mahdi.blogdrive.com/archive/" target=_top>http://mahdi.blogdrive.com/archive/</a> <BR> <BR>Here is a link to a blog that, after a bit of reading, states that Joseph Otero was shot with a gun. <BR> <BR>This is open to question, yet its the second time in as many days that I have heard new facts, important facts, about this case which has been the foundation of the investigation all along.  <BR> <BR>Yesterday I read that The younger joseph was tied to a chair and his head was covered with paper grocery bags. Apparently the police have been releasing as much misinformation as Btk. <BR> <BR>How they expect the public to cooperate with them is beyond me, when they obviously have no problem with lying about the facts to the public. <BR> <BR>The attitude of : don&#39;t rush out and buy guns to protect yourself, we got it under control,  ain&#39;t gonna hold water if they are gonna sit around waiting for more bodies to show up till they think they have enough clues to go on. <BR> <BR>Right now I am getting too pissed off to type what I&#39;m really starting to think about this investigation...so I going to take a break and Google some info. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10456-->
<!--Post: 10472--><!--Time: 1109968480-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10472"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 12:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Well, based on the timeline something sure doesn&#39;t add up.  How could Denny know there would be three dudes before there were three dudes in custody?  Could the three dudes have been the actual Otero murderers and given information to Denny so that he could write a convincing letter to get them off the hook?  &#40;The DNA from the scene should help answer that&#41;.  Or possibly one or more of the three dudes were with Denny that day at the Otero&#39;s?   <BR> <BR>I hope that somehow/someway/someday &#40;soon&#41; we&#39;ll get to find out EVERYTHING about this case and Denny.  I think a full disclosure could bring a lot of surprises. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10472-->
<!--Post: 10493--><!--Time: 1109973093-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10493"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 1:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is NO!!! DNA from the Otero murderscene, the condition of the DNA taken from the scene is not good enough for DNA testing. <BR>Le said that in a vido I saw yesterday and now I cant remember where it was I saw it, but it is 100% that the police said that. <BR> <BR>If they are telling the truth!!! <BR> <BR>OR do they say this because the DNA from the Otero murderscene doesn not fit Dennis Rader? <BR> <BR>And YES I belive raider know the dudes and that at least som of the dudes was at the Oteros. <BR> <BR>could the DNA be from one of the dudes?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10493-->
<!--Post: 10498--><!--Time: 1109973905-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10498"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kplynn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kplynn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 2:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In my opinion, BTK letter&#39;s mentioning the three dudes in no way implies that there were 3 people working with him.  There could have been, but I wouldn&#39;t base that possibility on the comment in his letter.  There were people claiming responsibility for the murder and he wanted everybody to know it was him.  The more likely scenario &#40;in my opinion&#41; is that two &#34;dudes&#34; were taken into custody, there was media buzz that there might be another taken, BTK heard about this and included &#34;three&#34; dudes in his communication.  I think it&#39;s very clear that the purpose of this letter was to make sure everyone knew HE, and he ALONE was responsible for this crime.  Now, please note, I&#39;m not definitely saying he did this alone, I don&#39;t know.  I&#39;m just saying I don&#39;t think his letter gives a strong argument that he did.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10498-->
<!--Post: 10507--><!--Time: 1109976976-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10507"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 2:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, what would really help is to see all the newspaper articles published for this time, but since im not in wichita...anybody want to go to the library?  <BR>Maybe there were 4 killers involved in the first one, and then they went off on their own, like a contest. That would explain all the differing eyewitness descriptions, and the different M.O.&#39;s, and moving the cars around, and if one of them ever got caught, one of the free ones could send a letter in to cops, proving that they had the wrong guy, since he couldnt be writing and mailing letters if he was in custody.  <BR>This is getting really far out there. <BR> <BR>If someone gets a letter now, since the arrest, I will completely freak out.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
