<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10533"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 5:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Police Await Oregon Report on Similarity in Otero Case  <BR>The Wichita Eagle April 4, 1974  <BR>&#40;no reporter name given&#41;  <BR> <BR>Wichita police said they should know &#34;Thursday or Friday&#34; if the man who turned himself in to Portland,  <BR>Ore., authorities Wednesday for the murders of four persons there was involved in the Otero murders here  <BR>Jan. 15.  <BR> <BR>Detective Capt. Charles Stewart said fingerprints of the suspect in Portland had been requested to compare  <BR>with ones found in the Joseph Otero home at 803 N. Edgemoor.  <BR> <BR>Colin Hockings, 30, of Gresham, Ore., turned himself in to the public defender in Portland when he learned  <BR>that warrants had been issued charging him with the March 25 killings of Howard A. Weeks, 29, his wife,  <BR>Arlene, 27, and two boys for whom they babysat, Kevin Wiebe, 7, and his brother, Todd, 9.  <BR> <BR>A staffer of the Portland Journal said Hockings had been charged with four counts of murder and was held  <BR>without bond.  <BR> <BR>Wichita detectives had been in contact with Portland officials since the slayings of the Oregon residents  <BR>because of the similarity between that case and the murders of Otero, 38, his wife, Julie, 34, daughter,  <BR>Josephine, 11, and son, Joseph II, 9.  <BR> <BR>In each case the victims were bound with material found in their homes, the crimes were committed early  <BR>in the morning - which local police said is most unusual - and the description of a man in the vicinity of  <BR>each murder scene was similar.  <BR> <BR>Robbery also was ruled out in each because the homes were not ransacked nor was there any sign of  <BR>a struggle in either residence. The victims were not sexually assaulted.  <BR> <BR>A dissimilarity in the two murders is the method in which the victims died. The Oteros were strangled and  <BR>the Portland victims were bludgeoned with a hammer.  <BR> <BR>The Journal spokesman said a motive for the Oregon slayings had not been determined late Wednesday  <BR>but apparently resulted from &#34;some kind of argument between Hockings and people who lived in the house &#40;the Weeks&#41;.&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10533-->
<!--Post: 10543--><!--Time: 1109994174-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10543"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 7:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Where did LE land on the Michael Williams Shooting. Did they ever make any arrests. He was a supervisor at Coleman who was shot in the same Basic area as the Otero house. Batin runs intermitently parallel to Edgemore within a few blocks. I&#39;m thinking that the house was in Bel Aire, yet another suburb, south of Kechi on Oliver. <BR> <BR>Police claimed that the shooting was unrelated to the Oteros. William&#39;s father &#40;head of HR at Coleman&#41;said it was a robbery attempt, although Michael Williams was Shot after opening the door and then closing it in the face of two assaillants, who shot him through the door with a shotgun. The &#34;TWO DUDE&#34; apparently made no attempt to force their way in, just BOOM. <BR> <BR>This occured Jan 12 1974, the Saturday preceeding the Otero Murder. Rader Quit Coleman sometime in 1973 and went to work at ADT. The article I read mentioned him enrolling at WSU in the fall of 73. <BR> <BR>Although the police denied a connection to the Otero case, I don&#39;t remember any mention of them questioning &#34;THE THREE DUDE&#34; in connection to the Williams shooting which may or may not be correct.  That would seem to be a faux pas. I don&#39;t remember that case being solved either. That also may be correct or not correct. <BR> <BR>If anyone has any good links on this i would be obliged.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10543-->
